    "1": {
      "note": "<em>cung2 mat6</em> (寵物) means pet, and the verb <strong>joeng5</strong> (養) covers raising or keeping any animal. The diminutive suffix <em>zai2</em> (仔) attaches to many small animals: <em>gau2 zai2</em> (狗仔, puppy), <em>maau1 zai2</em> (貓仔, kitten), <em>tou3 zai2</em> (兔仔, rabbit — the standard form). Note <strong>ngau4 juk6</strong> (牛肉, beef) and <strong>zyu1 juk6</strong> (豬肉, pork) — same animal words plus <em>juk6</em> (肉, meat).",
